       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Sertraline 1000 mg daily is far above the maximum recommended adult dose of 200 mg/day, and a dose that high risks serotonin syndrome, seizures, and QT prolongation. It may be a typo for 100 mg.\n\nCan you confirm the intended dose? Typical adult dosing is:\n- **Depression/anxiety:** start at 25\u201350 mg once daily, usually titrated to 50\u2013200 mg.\n- **Maximum:** 200 mg/day.\n\nOnce you give me the correct dose, I'll enter it right away. If 1000 mg is truly intended, for example as a deliberate exception, tell me and I'll note that on the order. I'd still recommend confirming with pharmacy first."
